Commit: 522fff8dcb526151c23f50f7545d207e07f9c843

@shuding 
hey, thanks for the review!
I am just gonna close this.

Hey! This upgrade causes yarn@berry to fail since there are multiple different patches on a shared dependency called `fsevents`.

```
➤ YN0066: │ fsevents@patch:fsevents@npm%3A2.3.2#builtin<compat/fsevents>::version=2.3.2&hash=127e8e: Cannot apply hunk #1
➤ YN0000: │     }
➤ YN0000: │   
➤ YN0028: │ -   let instance = Native.start(path, handler);
➤ YN0028: │ +   let VFS = require('./vfs');
➤ YN0028: │ +   let vfs = new VFS(path);
➤ YN0028: │ +   let instance = Native.start(vfs.resolvedPath, vfs.wrap(handler));
➤ YN0000: │     if (!instance) throw new Error(`could not watch: ${path}`);
➤ YN0000: │     return () => {
```

This `fsevents` package is included by several different libraries and for us it's an older version of `jest-haste-map` (24.9.0) and chokidar (included by babel-cli@6.26.0) that breaks it. Pretty sure that this could break on other systems as well. Will also report this on the yarn berry repo.

Resoluting `jest-haste-map` to `^26` fixes the issue for us and chokidar to `3.5.1` fixes it.

