Commit: 89437a04dce84f7034a8606c7f3d94bf3e9bf138

@Timer Just checking in to see if there's a way we can move this forward?

I still feel the [`isWindows`](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/blob/460c7c7ddcc55f9f15e43250b01f09e8385abc52/packages/next/build/webpack/config/blocks/base.ts#L25) check could be handed off to the user if required whilst keeping existing functionality in-tact, e.g.:

```
if (process.env.__NEXT_TEST_MODE && !process.env.__NEXT_TEST_WITH_DEVTOOL) {
      config.devtool = false
    } else if(ctx.unsafeDevToolOverride && ['inline-source-map', 'eval-source-map'].includes(ctx.unsafeDevToolOverride)) {
      config.devtool = ctx.unsafeDevToolOverride;
    } else if (isWindows) {
      // Non-eval based source maps are slow to rebuild, so we only enable
      // them for Windows. Unfortunately, eval source maps are flagged as
      // suspicious by Windows Defender and block HMR.
      config.devtool = 'inline-source-map'
    } else {
      // `eval-source-map` provides full-fidelity source maps for the
      // original source, including columns and original variable names.
      // This is desirable so the in-browser debugger can correctly pause
      // and show scoped variables with their original names.
      config.devtool = 'eval-source-map'
    }
```
If Windows users are forced to use `inline-source-map` then I see no reason why other users can't choose to use it if it suits their use case.
